// error
// #2773: `function` was the bootstrap-bridge spelling of `fn` (SPEC §10.3)
// for exactly one release, so compiler source still built by the previous
// stage0 (which parsed `function` only) kept compiling until a release
// carrying `fn` existed and the pin moved. The bridge is now closed:
// `function` lexes as an ordinary identifier, not a keyword. Dropping the
// lexer alias alone would leave a user with pre-#2773 source facing a
// generic "expected a top-level declaration" pointing at the word they wrote
// in good faith — the checker instead names `fn` as the replacement.
//
// What must STAY legal, in the same file: `fn main() {}`, entirely
// unaffected by the removal.
function old() {
}

fn main() {
}
